---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Install PENORA" description="Add PENORA to your phone’s home screen.">
  <section class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-5 py-12 space-y-7">
    <img src="/icons/penora-192.png" alt="PENORA" width="80" height="80" class="rounded-2xl" />
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-[#0A2540]">PENORA on your phone</h1>
    <p class="text-slate-600">Keep PENORA on your home screen for quick access to your wallet, stories and communities.</p>
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[#007C8B]/20 bg-white p-6 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Android</h2>
      <p>Open PENORA in Chrome, open the browser menu and choose <strong>Install app</strong> or <strong>Add to Home screen</strong>.</p>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">iPhone</h2>
      <p>Open PENORA in Safari, tap <strong>Share</strong>, then <strong>Add to Home Screen</strong>. Enable <strong>Open as Web App</strong> if shown.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-2xl bg-[#0A2540] text-white p-6 space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Using your wallet</h2>
      <p>The wallet currently uses Polygon Amoy testnet. To connect on mobile, open the PENORA wallet link inside your Web3 wallet’s built-in browser, such as MetaMask. Home-screen installation alone does not connect a wallet.</p>
      <p>Balances and transactions require a network connection. Keep your recovery phrase in your wallet; PENORA never asks for it.</p>
    </div>
    <a href="/wallet/" class="inline-block rounded-xl bg-[#007C8B] px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-white">Open PENORA Wallet</a>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
